\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces the overall pipeline of the proposed method.The object model is first reconstructed from the anchor image. With the proposed SPMG module, noisy point clouds are refined into high-quality geometric representations. A bounding box is then estimated from the filtered point cloud and used to rescale the reconstructed model, recovering its physical scale. Meanwhile, the pose of the anchor image is estimated using the FoundationPose~\cite  {wen2024foundationpose} framework.Subsequently, the pose of the query image is estimated using the same pose estimation method. By combining the two poses, the relative 6D pose between the anchor and query images is obtained.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{Fig. 2}{{2}{3}{}{figure.2}{}}
